# Fear of Being Hunted: "This creature must be blocked if able" (CR 509.1c). The requirement is one blocker on it, not every creature
# able to block (CR 509.1c: the most requirements obeyed, and one blocker obeys this one). Turn 3: it attacks with Elvish
# Mystic into Bot2's two Ornithopters. Both blocking the Mystic is refused (one of them could block the Fear), and so is no block
# at all; one Ornithopter on the Fear and the other on the Mystic is allowed. The Fear kills its Ornithopter, the Mystic is
# blocked by the other and deals it 1, which a 0/2 survives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Fear of Being Hunted
Elvish Mystic
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fear of Being Hunted.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Fear of Being Hunted > Bot2; Elvish Mystic > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Count: 0)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Elvish Mystic; Ornithopter#2 > Elvish Mystic)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Fear of Being Hunted; Ornithopter#2 > Elvish Mystic)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mox Emerald; Fear of Being Hunted; Elvish Mystic
